      "source": [
        "## Reader guide: end-to-end flow\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **YAML `model_params`** — `deepsets_inclusion_rule` selects which rule is written into each case `.pt` file. `deepsets_compare_inclusion_rules` lists extra rules evaluated in the same pass for metrics only.\n",
        "2. **`build_deepsets_dataset.py`** — For every case, each rule either keeps points that pass a signed-distance policy, uses **nearest 64** skeleton points as fallback (when the rule name ends with `_with_fallback` and the strict set is empty), or uses strict selection only (`local_radius_only`) / nearest-only (`nearest_64_only`).\n",
        "3. **`inclusion_rule_summary.csv`** — One row per rule with cohort aggregates: coverage (`cases_written` / `cases_skipped`), `fallback_fraction`, and point-count spread (`num_points_median`, `num_points_range` as `min-max`).\n",
        "4. **This notebook** — Loads that CSV, prints tables, draws the 2×2 figure panel (counts, fallback, median points with whiskers), and writes matching PNGs under `analysis/issue121_figures/` when you run the plotting cell.\n"
      ],
      "id": "issue121-md-pipeline"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Glossary: signed distance and each rule\n",
        "\n",
        "**Signed distance (mm)** is negative **inside** the tumor mask and positive **outside**; larger positive values are farther from the boundary along the vessel graph samples used in the build.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **`local_radius_with_fallback`** — Primary set: points with signed distance **≤ `local_radius_mm`**, where `local_radius_mm` comes from `deepsets_local_radius_floor_mm`, `deepsets_local_radius_scale`, `deepsets_local_radius_cap_mm`, and the case’s `tumor_equiv_radius_mm`. If that yields no points, keep the nearest 64 points by signed distance.\n",
        "- **`fixed_radius_30mm_with_fallback` / `fixed_radius_50mm_with_fallback`** — Primary set: signed distance **≤ 30 mm** or **≤ 50 mm** respectively; same nearest-64 fallback if empty.\n",
        "- **`peritumoral_shells_with_fallback`** — Primary set: **inside the tumor** (negative signed distance) **or** outside with signed distance **< 5 mm** (first shells only); same fallback if empty.\n",
        "- **`local_radius_only`** — Same tumor-relative cutoff as the default’s primary filter, **no** fallback; skipped cases highlight how many studies would drop out without rescue.\n",
        "- **`nearest_64_only`** — Always the 64 points with smallest signed distance (closest to the tumor), ignoring the local-radius cutoff; baseline for “always get a small set.”\n"
      ],
