        "## Reading the bar charts\n",
        "\n",
        "Each dataset block (fixture or cohort) produces **four** panels (2×2) with the\n",
        "same rules on the x-axis (short tick labels; full ids stay in the CSV).\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Cases written** counts how many cases survive under each rule. A rule that\n",
        "  writes far fewer cases than the default is a poor training default unless the\n",
        "  dropped cases are intentionally excluded.\n",
        "- **Cases skipped** counts case loss when the rule has no fallback. Compare this\n",
        "  panel to **Cases written** for fallback rules: large gaps between\n",
        "  `local_radius_only` and `local_radius_with_fallback` mean fallback is doing\n",
        "  real rescue work.\n",
        "- **Fallback fraction** applies to rules that allow fallback. Values near zero\n",
        "  mean the primary cutoff usually suffices. High values mean the rule often could\n",
        "  not find local points and had to widen the set via nearest neighbors.\n",
        "- **Median num_points** (purple bars) shows typical set size per rule; whiskers\n",
        "  span the min–max range from `num_points_range` in the CSV. Compare this panel\n",
        "  with **Fallback fraction** when judging locality vs breadth.\n",
        "\n",
        "Running the plotting cell also writes a high-DPI PNG under `analysis/issue121_figures/`\n",
        "for slides or side-by-side review. When comparing fixed-radius and peritumoral-shell\n",
        "variants, ask whether extra written cases come with acceptable fallback and point-count\n",
        "behavior, not whether more points is automatically better."
      ],
      "id": "f5de0cf27b2349ce"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-05-11T19:01:44.939043Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-05-11T19:01:44.938740Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-05-11T19:01:46.185015Z",
